See AGENTS.md for full project context, test strategy, and Bruno .bru file conventions.

Key rules:
- Always match llama-stack-client version to the server before running notebooks. Query server version, pin client in pyproject.toml (e.g., ==0.3.5), run uv sync. Use uv run for all Python/pytest commands.
- Notebook execution requires ipykernel in pyproject.toml deps. Always run uv sync before running notebooks.
- NEVER hardcode model names or provider-specific values. Models must come from variables ({{model}} in Bruno, MODEL env var in notebooks) with NO defaults. Embedding models use {{embedding_model}}. Only baseUrl/BASE_URL may have a default (http://localhost:8321).
- Never edit files in bruno/lls-api/ (auto-generated from OpenAPI)
- Add CRUD tests in bruno/lls-crud/NN-group/Action Resource.bru
- Use {{baseUrl}} (camelCase) for the server URL
- Always read the generated .bru file in lls-api/ before writing its CRUD counterpart
- Include script:post-response blocks with status and shape assertions
- Use bru.setEnvVar() to chain IDs between create/get/delete requests
- Use seq in meta to control execution order within folders
- Notebooks: assert on structure (types, fields), never on content (LLM output varies)
